  "classification": "subordinate finite original Wide relation return and actual Division consumer",
  "claim": "Two consecutive original Division input pairs supply the physical-slot K price difference. The original Gram quotient inverse synthesizes a Wide graph retaining both directed logs and both second conductor fields. The finite Cayley error separates the missing Gram closure energy in norm form and the damped tail proportional to (m+1)q^m. The diagonal recovers the original current and next stocks in the Wide norm.",
  "scope": "The actual 4+m operation programme ends with the native R write on the fitted graph. It generates the complete branch relation update and reads the next independent original K in the diagonal limit. Its runtime exposes the generated relation, inventory, whole and next under the original calculation occurrence. The direct consumer separately reads the original Division macro receipt.",
  "typed_control_scope": "Swapping the original bank pair negates the actual price difference. The full realized effect is nonzero by the exact original inverse and the nonzero original stock. At zero inverse rounds the recovered and next graphs vanish, so the recovery misses that stock.",
  "finite_original_stock_equality_claim": false,
